WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.166
Now.

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.201
78 year old

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.135
American citizen

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.003
has been sentenced

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.304
by a Chinese court

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.873
to life in prison on spying charges.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.008
John Liu,

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:08.942
who is also a Hong

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.210
Kong permanent resident

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.144
was detained

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.212
two years ago

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.681
by state security authorities.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.415
Authorities in Hong

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.516
Kong have been notified

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.184
and are now following up.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.285
China hasn't provided

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.121
any further details.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.122
The sentencing comes

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:22.689
as relations

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.224
between Beijing and Washington

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.027
are at their lowest point in 50 years.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.428
Ivan Watson joins us now.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:28.661
Ivan,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.396
when I read this story,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.096
I'm embarrassed to say

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.464
I hadn't even and didn't

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.565
recognize his name.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.134
What more do we know about him

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.603
and and the charges against him?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:38.171
Right.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:38.405
Well,

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:39.739
we really didn't know

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.940
that this American citizen

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.842
had been in Chinese custody

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.811
for four more than two years

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.280
until the court in Suzhou

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.348
issued this statement

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.382
today announcing

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.819
that he had been sentenced to life

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.955
imprisonment on the charge of espionage.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.324
They identified the man as John

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.861
Shin Wang, known 78 years old, a U.S.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.363
citizen, also

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.864
a Hong Kong permanent resident

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.266
who'd actually been

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:10.737
detained since April 15th of 2021.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.305
We don't have

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.140
really further details on that,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.842
except that the Hong Kong government,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.410
the highest security official in the Hong

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.678
Kong government,

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.948
did clarify in a press conference that

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.150
the administration here in

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.252
Hong Kong knew about this case

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.222
going back to 20, 21, but did not add

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.990
any further comments on this.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.159
Now we've reached out to the US Embassy

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.494
and they also say

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.228
that they're

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.530
not going to comment on this case

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.165
due to privacy considerations

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.868
and that they have no greater priority

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.903
than the safety and security of U.S.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.039
citizens overseas.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.741
I would like to add that just last week

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:49.442
the US

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.611
national security adviser Jake Sullivan,

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.080
he met for hours face to face with

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.349
his Chinese counterpart, Wang

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.051
Yi in Vienna.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.486
And they had discussed

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.321
a whole wide range of issues.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.423
But among the issues

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.991
that Sullivan reportedly

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:08.495
brought up were the cases of Americans

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.830
allegedly wrongfully detained

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.232
in Chinese custody.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.200
Marc, Sweden, Kylie and David Lin.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.002
We did not hear the name

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.937
of this individual

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.340
who's just received a life sentence

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.307
in China.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.742
One final detail

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.811
is that the Chinese government

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:28.014
has been tightening the rules

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.717
for what it defines as espionage.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.853
It passed a law making it much stricter

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.155
some years ago

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.990
and just last month has tightened

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.991
those rules

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.459
even more, making it

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.628
potentially very, very dangerous

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.663
to hold on to any documents,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.632
even any papers

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.801
that the authorities could judge to be

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.271
a national security matter.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.939
Yeah, I mean, this

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.774
there's so much detail in that.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:55.608
It's quite fascinating.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:56.776
And what stands out to me, actually,

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.711
is what you said about those talks.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.213
Several hours on one occasion,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.615
I think I read 8 hours worth of talks

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.150
between high level officials

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.751
and the choice here,

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.252
Jake Sullivan, rather than the U.S.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.420
secretary of state.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.855
Interesting timing,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.956
important breakthrough,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:10.890
given that I just said

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.125
in your introduction,

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.328
a 50 year low in relations, important to

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.664
to be around a table and talking

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.532
I think at this moment for many reasons.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:21.734
Absolutely.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.036
And also the fact

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.171
that I mean this was on Friday

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.340
that both the Chinese side

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.042
and the White House put out

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.077
remarkably similar statements

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.912
meaning that they for once

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.514
these two governments

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.615
their delegations were able

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.883
to come to agreement

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:37.951
and not just about that

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.118
but also to agree

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.187
that they would maintain

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.456
this important strategic channel

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.024
of communication.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.226
And one step further

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.127
that they would build on the engagement

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.128
between President

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.697
Biden and President Xi

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.698
that was reached

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.066
back in Bali

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.101
on the sidelines of the G-20 summit

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.704
in November. Of last year.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.072
That's not the kind of language

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.340
that we've heard in months

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.307
ever since that

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.243
that Chinese surveillance balloon

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.211
was detected over the US

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.046
and then shot down by the US.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.048
And that basically scuppered

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.683
a planned visit

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.151
by the US Secretary of State

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.153
Blinken to Beijing.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.522
It could be a sign these talks last week

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.824
that the two,

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:18.725
the world's two largest

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.727
economies are headed towards

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.262
some kind of

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.329
common ground,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.865
which would probably be welcome

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.600
if you're talking about stability

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.302
around the world. Absolutely.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.704
Watch this space and agree

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.972
on the

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.707
remarkably similar statements

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.943
to a movement here. Clearly, I think.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.244
Ivan Watson, thank you.

